change:
  id: CHG-024
  title: Held-out behaviour cases so task_success can discriminate between promoted candidates
  status: accepted
  intent: Let a promoted candidate score below 1.0 on task_success, so two candidates that both pass every required case remain comparable.
  audience_level: developer
  relates_to:
    - ADR-0002
    - CON-002
    - RISK-002
    - RISK-007
    - RISK-008
    - PAT-004
    - Q-004

deltas:
  - op: MODIFIED
    capability: mutation-fitness-loop
    requirement: A behaviour case may be held out, so that it runs and scores without deciding eligibility.
    scenarios:
      - id: S1
        when: a held-out case is declared
        then: its script is executed and its outcome recorded as check evidence
        and:
          - a declared case that produced no evidence is recorded as failed, so a held-out case that never ran would lower task_success from absence rather than measurement
          - execution is therefore asserted separately from scoring, and the scoring assertion is not trusted until it holds
      - id: S2
        when: every gating behaviour case passes and a held-out case fails
        then: task_success falls below 1.0 and the candidate is still eligible
        and:
          - the required_behavior_cases gate reads only the gating view of the behaviour cases
          - the deterministic_checks gate does not see the held-out case either, because a failing check would otherwise discard through the other gate
      - id: S3
        when: one gating case is declared beside one held-out case and the held-out case fails
        then: the raw magnitude falls below the 0.80 threshold and the candidate is discarded
        and:
          - task_success carries 0.40, so one failing case in n costs 0.40/n, which exceeds a typical promotion's headroom when n is 2
          - the discard is threshold arithmetic rather than a gate the held-out case tripped, so the ratio of held-out to gating cases governs both resolution and survivability
      - id: S6
        when: a fingerprinted record is written to the ledger or a Git envelope and read back
        then: the fingerprint survives, and a record written without one still reads as legacy
        and:
          - a fingerprint lost on reload would be worse than none, because the comparability filter would then exclude every reloaded record and the working set would be silently empty after a restart
      - id: S5
        when: a candidate is scored
        then: the result carries the fingerprint of the objectives, weights, withheld checks and threshold it was measured against
        and:
          - a result built without one reports legacy-unversioned rather than appearing comparable
          - the fingerprint is not backfilled for older records, because inventing one would fabricate provenance
      - id: S4
        when: a held-out name collides with a gating case, a safety probe, a structural gate or a derived repeat-run name
        then: the scoring configuration is rejected at construction
        and:
          - only the structural-gate rule is inherited; the other three are new, because until held-out cases no two declared name sets could name one check with different meanings

acceptance:
  - scenario: S1
    test_id: cli/EvolveCommandAcceptanceTest.executesADeclaredHeldOutCaseRatherThanScoringItFromAbsence
    layer: acceptance
  - scenario: S2
    test_id: cli/EvolveCommandAcceptanceTest.aFailingHeldOutCaseLowersTheScoreWithoutDiscardingTheCandidate
    layer: acceptance
  - scenario: S3
    test_id: cli/EvolveCommandAcceptanceTest.aThinGatingRatioLetsOneHeldOutFailureFallThroughThePromotionFloor
    layer: acceptance
  - scenario: S5
    test_id: domain/ScoringContextTest.changingTheHeldOutSetChangesTheFingerprint
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S5
    test_id: deterministic/ScorerStampsScoringContextTest.aScoredResultCarriesARealScoringContextRatherThanLegacy
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S5
    test_id: deterministic/ScorerStampsScoringContextTest.aResultBuiltWithoutAContextReportsLegacy
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S6
    test_id: adapters/ScoringFingerprintRoundTripIntegrationTest.theScoringFingerprintSurvivesTheSqliteLedger
    layer: integration
  - scenario: S6
    test_id: adapters/ScoringFingerprintRoundTripIntegrationTest.theScoringFingerprintSurvivesTheLedgerEnvelope
    layer: integration
  - scenario: S4
    test_id: deterministic/HeldOutCaseConfigTest.rejectsAHeldOutCaseThatIsAlsoAGatingBehaviourCase
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S4
    test_id: deterministic/HeldOutCaseConfigTest.rejectsAHeldOutCaseShapedLikeARepeatedRun
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S2
    test_id: deterministic/HeldOutCaseConfigTest.withholdsAHeldOutCaseFromTheGateWhileKeepingItInTheScoredList
    layer: unit

tasks:
  - id: T1
    slice: separate the gating view of behaviour cases from the scored list so a held-out case feeds task_success without gating
    status: completed
  - id: T2
    slice: execute declared held-out cases and bring them under the check-script guards
    status: completed
  - id: T3
    slice: reject held-out names that collide with another declared set
    status: completed
  - id: T4
    slice: unit-level coverage for ScoringConfig collision rules and PhenotypeEvidence.gatingBehaviorCases
    status: completed
  - id: T5
    slice: carry a ScoringContext fingerprint on FitnessResult and refuse comparison across differing fingerprints
    status: completed
  - id: T6
    slice: README, wiki and knowledge updates, including a RISK entry for held-out reliance on WORKFLOW_DEFINITION scope
    status: completed

non_goals:
  - population evaluation or ranking, which is CHG-025
  - renormalising the weighted sum over measured objectives only
  - changing the promotion threshold, the objective weights, or which cases gate
  - migrating local experiment data, which is derived and rebuilt

risks:
  - A held-out case is a script in the repository. It is out of a candidate's reach only because mutation scope is WORKFLOW_DEFINITION; requireWorkflowIsNotCheckScript alone does not protect it, so widening scope would make held-out cases mutable by the candidate they grade.
  - task_success resolution is 0.40/n. With few cases the objective two-bins candidates rather than ordering them finely, and ordering within a bin still falls back to parsimony.
